    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Ruben's revolt against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> in 1080 founded the principality; Levon II's coronation at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarsus">Tarsus</a> on 6 January 1198, backed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a>, made it a kingdom.</li><li>Het'um I's alliance with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>, sealed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karakorum">Karakorum</a> in 1250 and 1253, drew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> vengeance: Sis was sacked in 1266 and 40,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenians">Armenians</a> carried off.</li><li>Cilician society adopted Western feudalism, chivalry and French titles, and the Armenian alphabet gained two letters, Ֆ and Օ, from the contact.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marco-polo">Marco Polo</a> set out on his journey to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in 1271 from Ayas, the Cilician Armenian port where the Genoese held licensed warehouses and Italian was the language of trade.</p></aside>
    </section>

